From f9e614024d120882c77a9a3c31550630b65309cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Hill <ch6574@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:36:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VLAN: step the station's own group state machine

Minimal backport of the non-MLO part of upstream hostap commit
ace76dd0f9dcc ("VLAN: Use appropriate group instead of the default VLAN
group").

wpa_group_sm_step_links() stepped the default (VLAN 0) group state
machine instead of the group of the VLAN the station is bound to. After a
GTK rekey on a non-zero VLAN, the VLAN group therefore stayed in SETKEYS
once all stations had acknowledged group key message 2, and the new GTK
was only installed as the TX key at the next rekey. Stations that
(re)associated in between received the new GTK in the 4-way handshake and
could not decrypt group-addressed frames (mDNS, IPv6 RA/ND, ARP).

The MLO partner-link hunks of the upstream commit are not included, as
they depend on wpa_select_vlan_wpa_group() (upstream commit dd65e53c9 and
follow-ups), which is not present in this hostapd version.

OpenWrt main already contains this logic: commit 4abffae9b4e8
("hostapd: update to 2.12") moved hostapd to hostap_2_12, which includes
ace76dd0f9dcc, so wpa_group_sm_step_links() there uses sm->group. This
patch brings the same behaviour to openwrt-25.12 for non-MLO BSSs.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Hill <ch6574@gmail.com>
---

--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth.c
@@ -6118,7 +6118,7 @@ static void wpa_group_sm_step_links(stru
 
 	if (!sm || !sm->wpa_auth)
 		return;
-	wpa_group_sm_step(sm->wpa_auth, sm->wpa_auth->group);
+	wpa_group_sm_step(sm->wpa_auth, sm->group);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	for_each_sm_auth(sm, link_id) {
